## Purpose
Refresh the concise README and fictional GUI media to show the current action
and retained resume filename. Publish all completed dashboard and desktop
updates, qualify the matching Windows release and install it side by side.
Preserve private setup, earlier releases and independently running applications.

## Tasks
- [x] Establish explicit publication authority, an unused version and exact preservation boundaries.
- [x] Update existing fictional captures, screenshots and both walkthrough GIFs.
- [x] Review the actual media and align README, current guides and versioned release notes.
- [x] Review the complete public payload and run source release qualification.
- [x] Commit and push only reviewed files with verified repository-local attribution and required trailers.
- [x] Publish the matching version tag through the existing qualification-gated Windows pipeline.
- [x] Verify exact hosted source, qualification runs, notes and release assets.
- [x] Download and verify the actual assets and every extracted file before a new side-by-side installation.
- [x] Exercise the installed frozen GUI and CLI offline without using private runtime data.
- [x] Verify source-launcher, private-metadata and earlier-release preservation.
- [x] Reconcile the issue, Project status and persistent backlink.

## Acceptance criteria
- [x] Current fictional media visibly show operation icons/names and retained or replaced resume filenames.
- [x] README remains concise, captioned and explicit about offline demonstrations and source-only dashboard extras.
- [x] Package metadata, tag, hosted run and downloaded manifest identify the same exact release source.
- [x] Published source includes all completed dashboard improvements; the Windows package includes the native desktop updates.
- [x] All source release gates and actual installed-asset offline checks pass.
- [x] No private configuration, applicant values, runtime data, continuity or unrelated work is published.
- [x] Existing launcher/configuration and earlier installations remain intact; no independent application is restarted.
- [x] Publication and offline qualification are not presented as live LinkedIn, clean-machine or human acceptance.
- [x] One exact repository issue, one correctly staged Project item and a durable backlink represent this workstream.

## Completion evidence
At the start, cloud and checkout heads agreed. The prior stable releases were
v0.2.0, v0.2.1 and v0.2.2; the v0.2.3 tag and local version directory were absent.
The exact forty-six accumulated public payloads, twenty-nine prior tracking
records, selected private-file/native-preference metadata and six earlier
installed public entrypoints are baselined. Both effective Git identities are
the repository-local identity. The existing source launcher runs the checkout;
it does not fetch or select a release.
Thirteen PNGs and both looping GIFs are regenerated from fictional owned
widgets. Five focused capture cases pass. Actual media review catches and
corrects filename elision so the replacement resume is visibly different.
The final run GIF has nine frames over 17.8 seconds; the tutorial has seven
over 14.2 seconds. README links resolve, and existing counter anchors remain
stable. Updated guides and versioned release notes preserve source-extra and
offline-qualification boundaries.
An isolated public-source candidate passes Ruff, Black over 119 files, mypy
over 73 implementation files and all 868 tests. No private runtime inputs or
unrelated plugin are copied into that lane.
Exactly sixty-five reviewed public files are published as source commit
c070dda81ab7a34671a010c527b3dfa082d1fac2 with the matching annotated v0.2.3
tag, verified local attribution and required session trailers. Independent
hosted read-back verifies the canonical tree, every payload blob, all fifteen
media assets and the actual README.
Both exact-source qualification runs succeed:
https://github.com/Zanark/LinkedIn-EasyApply-Automaton/actions/runs/42736325477
https://github.com/Zanark/LinkedIn-EasyApply-Automaton/actions/runs/42736325565
The main run correctly skips publication; the tag run publishes the three
Windows assets. The latest stable release is
https://github.com/Zanark/LinkedIn-EasyApply-Automaton/releases/tag/v0.2.3
Its notes match the reviewed versioned document exactly.
The actual downloaded ZIP, manifest and checksums match hosted sizes/digests.
The manifest identifies the exact release source, all 450 extracted files
verify, and a fresh side-by-side installation retains the 21-topic tutorial.
Eight actual installed offline checks cover CLI commands, fictional exports
and native GUI, Playwright driver and sibling-command integration. The
installed version is exactly 0.2.3; all 450 files verify again afterward.
Selected private/native metadata, the source launcher and six earlier
installed entrypoints are unchanged. All three earlier public tags, release
identities and nine hosted assets remain intact. No independent application
is restarted. Dashboard and AI remain source extras; the portable download
does not acquire those capabilities. Offline checks are not live LinkedIn,
clean-machine or human acceptance. Scoped issue, Project and backlink
settlement is independently recorded in the index and development ledger.

